  "instruction": "Identify the five countries that had the greatest share of reduction in reported TB cases in 2021 compared to 2019. Of these countries, which reported the lowest number of TB cases in 2023?",
  "answer": "Based on my research, here's the answer:\n\n## Five countries with the greatest share of reduction in reported TB cases in 2021 vs 2019\n\n**India, Indonesia, China, Myanmar, and the Philippines** — these five countries accounted for **90% of the global reduction in TB case notifications in 2021 compared to 2019**, according to the WHO Global Tuberculosis Report (cited in CIDRAP and WHO sources).\n\n## Which of these five reported the lowest number of TB cases in 2023?\n\n**Myanmar** reported the lowest number of TB cases in 2023 among these five countries.\n\n**2023 notified TB case numbers (new and relapse):**\n- India: **2.55 million** (25.52 lakh) — *India TB Report 2024 / PIB*\n- Indonesia: **~821,200** — *Statista/WHO data*\n- China: **~700,000+** (estimated notifications; exact figure not directly published but higher than Myanmar)\n- Philippines: **612,534** — *Philippines health authorities / WHO*\n- Myanmar: **125,954** — *Myanmar TB Programmatic Achievement 2023 (The Global Fund Programme in Myanmar)*\n\nMyanmar's 2023 notifications (~126,000) are substantially lower than the other four countries.",
  "answer_chars": 1108,
  "expected_answer": "Myanmar",
